{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/892447-dark-eras-how-do-you-introduce-players-to-the-world-they-live-in","id":892447,"title":"Dark Eras - How do you introduce players to the world they live in?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-17T06:12:47-07:00","id":892447,"title":"Dark Eras - How do you introduce players to the world they live in?","content":"I don't expect my players to read the chapter, and in fact doing so might expose some mysteries I don't want them to know. That said outside of any 20th century eras and especially neolithic the world can be quite different.<br /> <br /> How do you go about explaining this world they live in? how do you avoid them tripping over things their characters would know but they don't? I suppose this is always somewhat of a problem even when running in modern nights but to a lesser extent. It's not one I've ever really figured out a great solution for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T06:49:36-07:00","id":892459,"title":"","content":"I'm prepping to do Sundered World as well, what I've done is discussed the differences in the setting with my players and shared some articles on the Vinca. Moving from there I wrote up a fictional valley of associated communities of the People with some short interesting but mostly mortal tidbits about them.<br /> <br /> For the first night I plan to have some talking points to help people get into character such as a piece of gossip about what's going on in their towns and to talk about their experiences with the Wise (my players are starting mortal to get a feel for the setting and will then Awaken due to a Deus Ex plot point.) We will play through traveling to a festival in the dominant settlement and trying to navigate the wilderness while encountering some mundane and low end supernatural dangers such as a low ranked spirit claiming an animal or tree.<br /> <br /> I'm making the chapter available to them and just expecting that they separate player knowledge and character knowledge as well as making sure I am mysterious enough in my descriptions to not give important things away. My players do this sort of thing very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","user":"The Cowardly Scion","date":". 05-17-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:13:48-07:00","id":892813,"title":"","content":"Just like any other game, I heavily suggest doing a &quot;session zero&quot; dedicated to character creation, hashing out expectations, and explaining the setting you'll be dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T13:48:57-07:00","id":893571,"title":"","content":"I gave my players a brief list of what was going on at the time, major events, that sort of thing. We spent a session making characters, establishing what the world was like at that point in history. As Atamajakki said session zeros work well for all Chronicles of Darkness games but especially for Dark Eras games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11247-bluenose","name":"Bluenose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T14:23:01-07:00","id":893596,"title":"","content":"One thing to consider is that the average person is not a history nerd, having suffered through how terrible most public education seems to be, and that the prospect of a historical setting can either fill them with dread or at least feel overwhelming. Reining in your scope and having a punchy pitch can do wonders for a playgroup that feels lost or unexcited; &quot;Mage in the Hellenistic Era&quot; means nothing to most people, but &quot;you're the power-players in the occult undergground of Babylon as the known world is divided up by hungry generals in the aftermath of the divine conqueror's death - and possible assassination!&quot; is far more gripping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:19:48-07:00","id":893798,"title":"","content":"It's not an absolute but the odds are pretty good that whatever era you pick there has been a book or movie that presents at least a portion of it, and even if your players haven't seen or read it the odds are they have some ideas about it. For example I'm betting a lot of the people on this forum haven't sat through all of Ben-Hur, but I'm also willing to bet that everyone reading this suddenly had the image of Charelton Heston racing in a chariot.<br /> \u200bSee if you can find such for your era, even if all the internet can give you are trailers and images it will give your players a feel for the setting upon which you can hang the details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}